' A real, ordinary ArcoBASIC program meant to be compiled BY the Fission
' Compiler Substrate's native x86-64 backend (fission/amir/lower_x86_64.abas)
' -- see fission/tests/native_programs/hello_native.abas's own header
' comment for the directory convention. Exercises ForEach (`FOR item IN
' values ... NEXT`) over a real array -- unblocked by Phase 7 (numeric
' arrays) landing, and confirmed to need zero dedicated native x86-64
' codegen at all, the same "already works" precedent FOR-range and DO
' loops already set: ForEach desugars entirely (in the SHARED
' fission/sir/lower_amir.abas pass, used by both backends) into the same
' Store/Const/Load/Call(LEN)/BinOp/Branch/Jump/Index primitives this
' backend already lowered for other constructs.
'
' Expected output verified against legacy `ArcoFission compile-run` on this
' identical source as the equivalence-testing oracle.
nums = [10, 20, 30]
FOR n IN nums
    PRINT n
NEXT

total = 0
FOR n IN nums
    total = total + n
NEXT
PRINT total

FUNCTION Double(x)
    RETURN x * 2
END FUNCTION

squares = [1, 4, 9, 16, 25]
FOR s IN squares
    PRINT Double(s)
NEXT
